{
  "dom_id": "step-e12752",
  "name": "Example: Expressing a Plain English Sentence With Two Quantifiers as a Formal Statement",
  "problem": "Express the following statement in formal language.\n\nFor each natural number, there is an integer such that their sum is $2.$",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The word \"each\" indicates that we use a universal quantifier, $\\forall.$\n\n- The words \"there is\" indicate that we use an existential quantifier, $\\exists.$\n\n- The sentence refers to a natural number and an integer number. So, by denoting our numbers as $n$ and $k,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\\forall \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, \\, \\exists \\, k \\in \\mathbb{Z}.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nn + k = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$\\forall \\, n \\in \\mathbb{N}, \\, \\exists \\, k \\in \\mathbb{Z}, \\, n + k = 2$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
